== Notes ==

* Added in the [[expansion pack]]s.
* The innate level is incorrectly reported as 3 by the in-game description.
* ''Continual flame'' is not removed by dispelling.
*When used on an item, this spell increases its price as it adds a permanent [[item property]]. This can be exploited for gold, by casting ''continual flame'' on every item that will be sold to a [[merchant]]. Many [[server]]s disallow this exploit, especially when the item in question was bought solely for the purpose of enchanting then selling at a profit.
* In [[pen and paper]], ''continual flame'' is in the [[evocation]] spell school, so some consider it a bug that [[BioWare]] has classified this spell as illusion.
* When cast on a creature, the effect of this spell prevents use of the [[shadowblend]] ability.

